<div id="2026-09-02-hdry-wheel-bom-and-fls02" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-02 — wheel kit BOM built, FLS02 recovered, queue gap-filled</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Wheel kit BOM.</strong> The kit (item 99, <code>HW-WHEEL-KIT</code>) previously listed <b>hardware only</b> &mdash; washer, bolt+nut, spacer &mdash; with no printed lines. That is why the support structure never reached the queue. Created 3 inventory items and added them:
<code>INT-HDRY-WHEEL-HALF</code> &times;8, <code>INT-HDRY-WHEEL-FOOT</code> &times;4, <code>INT-HDRY-WHEEL-TIRE</code> &times;4 (per user: 1 wheel = 2 halves + 1 tire, 4 wheels, foot 1 per wheel).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Circular BOM caught.</strong> Model 48 ("HDRY printed wheels (set of 4)") was linked to <code>item_id = 99</code> &mdash; and item 99 <em>is</em> the wheel kit. Adding a BOM line 99&rarr;99 would have made the kit a component of itself. Detected before writing; model 48 was repointed to the new wheel-half item (108). <code>hdry_make_wheel_items.pl</code> now skips any line that would be circular.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>FLS02 recovered from the 3MF.</strong> Model 31 had no <code>nfs_path</code>. The file <code>FLS02_.stl</code> exists in both module dirs; confirmed as the mirror of <code>FRS02.stl</code> (chamfer 1.589 mirrored vs 9.158 direct, 5.8x separation, identical 20&times;172&times;215 bbox). Linked at 215 mm / 403.63 cm&sup3; and queued &mdash; no re-download from the 3MF needed.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Queue gap-filled.</strong> Note on why manual action was required: <code>/3d/queue_sync</code> reports nothing needed because it compares against BOM lines, and several BOM lines were themselves wrong or missing (kit had no printed lines; FLS02 was unlinked). Sync is only as good as the BOM. Queue now <b>32 jobs / 67 units</b>, zero duplicates.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Schema drift found.</strong> <code>inventory_items</code> has no <code>is_active</code> column (the Result class declares one) &mdash; active-ness is <code>status</code>, default <code>'active'</code>. Also <code>hide_stock_count</code> and <code>show_in_shop</code> are NOT NULL with no default and must be supplied on INSERT. Recorded here because <code>_create_item()</code> cannot be called from CLI (needs <code>$c-&gt;model</code>); scripts insert directly.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> New <code>script/hdry_make_wheel_items.pl</code> and <code>script/hdry_fill_gaps.pl</code> (both idempotent, dry-run default).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Still blocked (see 2026-09-10 diagnosis).</strong> HDry Lite Desiccant Box (model 16) &mdash; path points at <code>/data/nfs/3d/projects/hdry-v3/141256_...3mf</code> which no longer exists; the source 3MF is only in <code>~/Downloads</code>. Needs re-import or path correction. Three wrongly-printed parts (#58 BBR01, #61 BR01, #63 FL01) still need reprinting. General root cause (stale <code>printing_3d_models.nfs_path</code> post-NFS restructure) diagnosed in auto-error-audit; full work order in <code>.hermes/plans/2026-09-10-3d-model-download-stale-nfs-path.md</code>. Use <code>model_upload</code> for remediation.</p>
</div>
